# 1️⃣ Count Even Numbers in an Array

### 💡 Problem

Count how many even numbers are present in an array.

```java
package p2;

public class CountEvenNum {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int[] arr = {2, 7, 4, 9, 6, 3};
        int count = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {

            if (arr[i] % 2 == 0) {
                count++;
            }
        }

        System.out.println("Count = " + count);
    }
}
```

### Output

```text
Count = 3
```

### 🔍 Dry Run

```text
2 → even → count = 1
7 → odd
4 → even → count = 2
9 → odd
6 → even → count = 3
3 → odd
```

### 🧠 Key Logic

```java
arr[i] % 2 == 0
```

means the element is even.

### ⏱ Complexity

* Time: `O(n)`
* Space: `O(1)`

### 🎯 Interview Tip

The pattern:

```java
if (condition) {
    count++;
}
```

is one of the most basic and important array patterns.

