# 2️⃣ Sum of Even Numbers

### 💡 Problem

Find the sum of all even elements.

```java
package p2;

public class SumOfEvenNum {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int[] arr = {2, 7, 4, 9, 6, 3};
        int sum = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {

            if (arr[i] % 2 == 0) {
                sum = sum + arr[i];
            }
        }

        System.out.println("Sum = " + sum);
    }
}
```

### Output

```text
Sum = 12
```

### 🔍 Dry Run

```text
2 → even → sum = 2
7 → odd
4 → even → sum = 6
9 → odd
6 → even → sum = 12
3 → odd
```

### 🧠 Key Pattern

Counting:

```java
count++;
```

Summing:

```java
sum = sum + arr[i];
```

### ⏱ Complexity

* Time: `O(n)`
* Space: `O(1)`

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

# 3️⃣ Find the Largest Even Number

### 💡 Problem

Find the largest even number in an array.

```java
package p2;

public class LargestEvenNum {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int[] arr = {12, 7, 24, 9, 16, 3};
        int largest = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {

            if (arr[i] % 2 == 0 && arr[i] > largest) {
                largest = arr[i];
            }
        }

        System.out.println("Largest Even = " + largest);
    }
}
```

### Output

```text
Largest Even = 24
```

### 🔍 Dry Run

```text
largest = 0

12 → even → 12 > 0 → largest = 12
7  → odd
24 → even → 24 > 12 → largest = 24
9  → odd
16 → even → 16 < 24
3  → odd
```

### 🧠 Key Pattern

Combine filtering and maximum finding:

```java
if (arr[i] % 2 == 0 && arr[i] > largest) {
    largest = arr[i];
}
```

### ⏱ Complexity

* Time: `O(n)`
* Space: `O(1)`

### ⚠️ Note

Initializing `largest = 0` works when the array contains positive even numbers. For a completely general array that may contain negative values, a safer approach is to initialize appropriately or handle the first valid even element separately.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

# 4️⃣ Find the Smallest Odd Number

### 💡 Problem

Find the smallest odd number.

```java
package p2;

public class SmallestOddNum {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int[] arr = {12, 7, 24, 9, 16, 3};
        int smallest = Integer.MAX_VALUE;

        for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {

            if (arr[i] % 2 != 0 && arr[i] < smallest) {
                smallest = arr[i];
            }
        }

        System.out.println("Smallest Odd = " + smallest);
    }
}
```

### Output

```text
Smallest Odd = 3
```

### 🧠 Why `Integer.MAX_VALUE`?

We don't know beforehand what the smallest odd number will be.

So we start with a very large value:

```java
int smallest = Integer.MAX_VALUE;
```

Then any valid odd number can replace it.

### 🔍 Dry Run

```text
12 → even → skip
7  → odd → smallest = 7
24 → even → skip
9  → odd → 9 < 7? No
16 → even → skip
3  → odd → 3 < 7 → smallest = 3
```

### ⏱ Complexity

* Time: `O(n)`
* Space: `O(1)`

### 🎯 Interview Tip

For minimum problems:

```java
Integer.MAX_VALUE
```

For maximum problems:

```java
Integer.MIN_VALUE
```

are common initialization techniques.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

# 5️⃣ Count Occurrences of an Element

### 💡 Problem

Count how many times a target appears.

```java
package p2;

public class CountOccurencesOfEle {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int[] arr = {2, 5, 2, 7, 2, 9, 5};
        int target = 2;
        int count = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {

            if (arr[i] == target) {
                count++;
            }
        }

        System.out.println("Occurrences = " + count);
    }
}
```

### Output

```text
Occurrences = 3
```

### 🔍 Dry Run

```text
2 → match → count = 1
5 → no
2 → match → count = 2
7 → no
2 → match → count = 3
9 → no
5 → no
```

### 🧠 Important Pattern

Whenever the question says:

> "How many times does X appear?"

Think:

```java
int count = 0;

if (arr[i] == target) {
    count++;
}
```

### ⏱ Complexity

* Time: `O(n)`
* Space: `O(1)`

